ity\",\n        \"F-config\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-abort\",\n        \"S-ack\",\n        \"S-advance\",\n        \"S-authority\",\n        \"S-bootstrap\",\n        \"S-changer\",\n        \"S-config\",\n        \"S-configapply\",\n        \"S-dispatch\",\n        \"S-jointcontract\",\n        \"S-majority\",\n        \"S-quorum\",\n        \"S-ready\",\n        \"S-readycontract\",\n        \"S-rolehandlers\",\n        \"S-send\",\n        \"S-storage\",\n        \"S-storagecontract\",\n        \"S-tally\",\n        \"S-ticks\",\n        \"S-transition\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Membership qualifies both election and replication support. Term resets discard old match/vote/readOnly acknowledgment tracking; Step rejects stale responses, while previously committed history remains binding. Entry stability acknowledgments retain the producing term to avoid discarding a replaced unstable suffix; old snapshot completions remain meaningful because snapshots carry committed state. Restart loads durable history/configuration and enters follower state. Pending pre-commit reads live separately from the reset readOnly queue and are released on response-based current-term commit. Applied membership may reinterpret existing matches and produce a commit without that same read-release callback. Application completion can propose automatic joint exit, but transfer admission can reject that proposal; these local continuation questions do not prevent understanding the backbone.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-election\",\n        \"B-leadercommit\",\n        \"B-config\",\n        \"B-durability\",\n        \"B-recovery\",\n        \"B-apply\",\n        \"B-autoleave\",\n        \"B-read\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-authority\",\n        \"F-commit\",\n        \"F-config\",\n        \"F-applied\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-ack\",\n        \"S-advance\",\n        \"S-ap